            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"God's Word, truth, and divine guidance providing spiritual direction in darkness.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Psalm 119:105\",\"Proverbs 6:23\",\"2 Peter 1:19\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"The visible witness, good works, and testimony of believers or the Church to the world.\",\"basis\":[\"Matthew 5:15\",\"Luke 8:16\",\"Revelation 1:20\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"The life, vitality, and enduring royal lineage of David.\",\"basis\":[\"1 Kings 11:36\",\"2 Samuel 21:17\",\"Psalm 132:17\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"The Holy Spirit or the manifest presence of God (often depicted as seven lamps).\",\"basis\":[\"Revelation 4:5\",\"Zechariah 4:2\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"The human spirit or conscience searching the inner being.\",\"basis\":[\"Proverbs 20:27\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"The symbolism of a lamp is well-established but polyvalent. While God's Word is the most ubiquitous association in popular piety due to Psalm 119:105, the lamp frequently represents the enduring Davidic dynasty in the Old Testament and the visible witness of believers in the New Testament.\"}",
